--TEST--
a `revoke()` call resolves to the member `Revocable` declares, so it answers that member's line and card, `rule:classes/revocable-objects`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Post implements Revocable {
    public function constructor(public string $title) {}
}

var $post = new Post('Hello');
$post->rev<|>oke();
--REQUEST--
hover
--EXPECT--
```nvs
Revocable::revoke(): void
```

Revokes this object and removes it from every `Core\ObjectMap`, `Core\ObjectSet` and `Core\Heap`. After that, a property read or a method call throws `RevokedObjectError`. A second call does nothing.
